The network backend startup hook is a modified Rust adaptation of a portion of
KytyPS5-Performance.

Source project: https://github.com/WerrySs/KytyPS5-Performance
Pinned source: 209dffe9032d72749257ce18680d506b891284de
Upstream project: https://github.com/KytyPS5/KytyPS5

Adapted source:
  src/libs/network.cpp, Net::EnsureSocketBackend and NetInit: Windows
  WSAStartup(MAKEWORD(2, 2)), retaining successful initialization and allowing
  retry after failure. The guest NetInit wrapper preserves the pinned zero
  return even if platform initialization fails. PentaX exposes this operation
  through its checked platform boundary;
  no guest integer is converted to a host function or socket pointer.

This hook performs actual backend initialization only. It does not create a
connection, execute DNS, allocate guest network pools or send/receive packets.
The pinned NetTerm performs no cleanup and has no registration in the reviewed
libNet.cpp export table; no WSACleanup behavior is attributed to it.

